raye-store (0.5~beta1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * An install that was not allowed now says it needs root access.
  * FL Studio and other music programs are filed under Audio, not
    Graphics.
  * Windows programs' shortcuts are read up to their end mark, as
    Windows does, and a removed space takes its hidden runner entry with
    it.
  * American spelling: License, Canceling, Canceled.
  * The Store offers popular Windows programs (WinRAR, 7-Zip, Notepad++,
    FL Studio, Roblox Studio) from their makers' own installers, checked
    against a pinned SHA-256 before anything runs.
  * Each Windows program says how it runs here: Optimized for Raye, Works
    on Raye, or Doesn't work on Raye for games whose anti-cheat refuses
    this system, with the reason. Those games stay out of Start menu
    search.
  * Searching for Discord, Steam, OBS, Minecraft, Spotify, Chrome, VLC or
    Epic Games finds the native app.
  * New home rows: Optimized for Raye and Your Windows favorites.
  * The big picture on top of Home and Apps shows apps most people know,
    picked by Raye (Firefox, Discord, Steam, OBS, GIMP and more), another
    one each day, instead of Flathub's picks.
  * A Windows program's install says "Installing…" and, on its own line,
    to finish in the setup window, instead of a line cut short.

